---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';
import { stats } from '../data/servers';
import SupportBand from '../components/SupportBand.astro';
import TelegramCta from '../components/TelegramCta.astro';
const st = stats();
---
<Layout title="About" description={`${brand.name}: ${brand.tagline} Open-source MCP servers for back-office work.`}>
  <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden">
    <div class="grid-lines"></div>
    <div class="wrap max-w-3xl pb-16 pt-14 sm:pt-20">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1 class="display mt-5 !text-[clamp(2.3rem,6vw,4.2rem)]">{brand.tagline}</h1>
      <div class="prose-site lead mt-8">
        <p>Most back-office work is small, repeated and boring: an invoice, a quote, a mileage log, a check that a supplier bill matches the order. You already ask an AI for help with words. {brand.name} lets it do the work and hand you the file.</p>
        <p>We build {st.servers} focused MCP servers. Each one does one job, and every tool is listed in its SPEC.md. {st.hosted} of them run as a hosted URL. All of them run on your own machine.</p>
        <p>The free tier needs no key. Pro is a one-time payment. The source is on <a href={brand.links.github} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a href="/servers/" class="btn btn-primary">Browse servers</a><a href="/developers/" class="btn">For developers</a></div>
      <p class="muted mt-8 text-[.97rem]">Want a server for your own API, spreadsheet or docs? The maintainer takes custom work. <a href="/services/" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">See custom work</a>.</p>
      <div class="mt-8"><TelegramCta /></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <SupportBand page="about" />
</Layout>
